---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import LifecycleNotice from "../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj12.json";
---
<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc items={[
        {id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage"},
        {id: "s2", label: "Scope — the Historical Quarterly Regime"},
        {id: "s3", label: "Why Quarterly Reporting Was Introduced"},
        {id: "s4", label: "Cumulative vs Single-Quarter Presentation"},
        {id: "s5", label: "The 2024–2025 Reform — Moving Toward Semi-Annual Reporting"},
        {id: "s6", label: "Integration With Stock Exchange Summary Disclosure"},
        {id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — the Historical Quarterly Regime in Outline"},
        {id: "s8", label: "Current Treatment — ASBJ Statement No. 37"},
        {id: "s9", label: "Disclosure Requirements (Current, Post-Reform)"},
        {id: "s10", label: "Critical Judgments"},
        {id: "s11", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS"},
        {id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping"},
        {id: "s13", label: "Related Standards"},
        {id: "s14", label: "Glossary"}
    ]} />
  </Fragment>

  <LifecycleNotice
    type="revised"
    title="Revised Standard"
    explanation="ASBJ has recently (2026) issued a revision to this Statement. The core historical framework described below is well-established, but the precise substance of the most recent revision should be verified against ASBJ's current published materials."
    link="/japangaap/asbj12"
    linkText="ASBJ Statement No. 12 — Accounting Standard for Financial Instruments"
  />

  <div class="wrap">

<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A once-mandatory regime, now folded into a lighter-touch semi-annual framework</div><div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 12 HISTORICALLY established Japan's MANDATORY quarterly financial reporting regime for listed companies — introduced following EARLY-2000s reforms to the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act (金融商品取引法) requiring listed companies to report FOUR times a year rather than just semi-annually or annually. This regime has since been LARGELY SUPERSEDED as part of a broader REGULATORY reform reducing the statutory reporting BURDEN, moving TOWARD semi-annual (interim) reporting instead.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — the Historical Quarterly Regime</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Listed companies filing quarterly reports</div><div class="principle">This Statement HISTORICALLY applied to LISTED companies required to file QUARTERLY reports (四半期報告書) under the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act, covering each of the first three quarters of the fiscal year (the fourth quarter being effectively covered by the ANNUAL report).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Why Quarterly Reporting Was Introduced</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Enhanced investor transparency, following international disclosure trends</div><div class="text-supporting">MANDATORY quarterly reporting was introduced to give INVESTORS more FREQUENT, TIMELY insight into a listed company's financial performance and position — REDUCING the information gap between annual (and previously semi-annual) reports, broadly FOLLOWING international disclosure trends toward more FREQUENT interim reporting seen in other major capital markets at the time.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Cumulative vs Single-Quarter Presentation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Two acceptable presentation approaches for the income statement</div><div class="text-supporting">Companies could present quarterly results EITHER on a CUMULATIVE basis (year-to-date figures, e.g. the first six months for the second quarter) OR on a SINGLE-QUARTER basis (results for THAT quarter alone) — with the CUMULATIVE approach being the MORE COMMONLY adopted method in practice.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>The 2024–2025 Reform — Moving Toward Semi-Annual Reporting</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A deliberate reduction in the statutory reporting burden</div><div class="text-supporting">As part of a BROADER disclosure reform, Japan MOVED AWAY from requiring FULL statutory quarterly financial statements for the FIRST and THIRD quarters, toward a LIGHTER-TOUCH regime centred on SEMI-ANNUAL (interim, second-quarter) statutory reporting instead — REFLECTED first in <strong>ASBJ Statement No. 33</strong> (Semi-annual Financial Reporting), and SUBSEQUENTLY REWORKED into <strong>ASBJ Statement No. 37</strong> (Interim Financial Reporting) — a genuinely SIGNIFICANT reduction in the STATUTORY reporting burden for listed companies, reflecting a POLICY judgement that quarterly stock-exchange summary disclosure (Section 6) already provides SUFFICIENT timely information WITHOUT requiring a FULL, separately-standardised statutory quarterly financial statement filing for every quarter.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Integration With Stock Exchange Summary Disclosure</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">"Kessan Tanshin" continuing to provide quarterly market disclosure</div><div class="text-supporting">SEPARATELY from the STATUTORY financial reporting regime, Japanese stock exchanges (notably the Tokyo Stock Exchange) have LONG required listed companies to release a "KESSAN TANSHIN" (決算短信) — a SUMMARY earnings disclosure — on a QUARTERLY basis, under exchange LISTING RULES rather than the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act itself. The 2024–2025 reform's REDUCTION of the FULL statutory quarterly reporting burden was DESIGNED to work ALONGSIDE this CONTINUING exchange-level quarterly summary disclosure, avoiding DUPLICATIVE reporting obligations.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — the Historical Quarterly Regime in Outline</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Filing a first-quarter report under the old regime</div>
<div class="worked worked--flush"><div class="wk-title">Example: A listed company's Q1 filing before the reform</div><div class="wk-body">A listed Japanese company, under the OLD regime, filed a quarterly report for its first fiscal quarter, presenting condensed financial statements on a cumulative basis.</div><div class="wk-answer">TODAY, the SAME company would generally NOT be required to file a FULL statutory quarterly report for that FIRST quarter — its PRIMARY statutory reporting obligation now centres on the SEMI-ANNUAL (second-quarter) interim report under <strong>ASBJ Statement No. 37</strong>, with QUARTERLY market transparency continuing to be served through its exchange-mandated "kessan tanshin" summary disclosure instead.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Current Treatment — ASBJ Statement No. 37</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Interim Financial Reporting as the current primary framework</div><div class="text-supporting">Today, LISTED companies apply <strong>ASBJ Statement No. 37, Interim Financial Reporting</strong>, for their SEMI-ANNUAL statutory reporting obligation — the CURRENT successor to this Statement's original quarterly regime, reflecting the genuinely REDUCED statutory reporting frequency now in force.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements (Current, Post-Reform)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What applies today instead</div><div class="check-list"><span>Semi-annual (interim) statutory financial statements under ASBJ Statement No. 37</span><span>Continuing quarterly "kessan tanshin" summary disclosure under stock exchange listing rules</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most (historically and today)</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">HISTORICAL JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether to present quarterly results on a cumulative or single-quarter basis</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">CURRENT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Materiality assessment for the semi-annual interim period under ASBJ Statement No. 37</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP's reformed regime vs IAS 34</div><div class="text-supporting">IAS 34 (Interim Financial Reporting) does NOT itself MANDATE any particular reporting FREQUENCY — it applies WHENEVER an entity prepares an interim report, WHETHER quarterly, semi-annual, or otherwise, leaving the FREQUENCY decision to LOCAL regulatory requirements. Japan's SHIFT from mandatory quarterly to semi-annual statutory reporting is therefore a change in LOCAL REGULATORY POLICY, not a divergence from any SPECIFIC IFRS frequency requirement — IAS 34's PRINCIPLES (condensed statements, consistent accounting policies, materiality assessed at the interim level) remain broadly APPLICABLE regardless of which frequency a jurisdiction chooses.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where interim/quarterly reporting now lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Semi-annual statutory reporting</span><span>All condensed statements</span><span>Governed by the current ASBJ Statement No. 37</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 33 / No. 37</span><span>Successor standards — the current semi-annual (interim) financial reporting framework</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Kessan Tanshin (決算短信)</div><div class="glossary-def">A stock exchange listing rule-mandated summary earnings disclosure, released quarterly, continuing independently of the reduced statutory quarterly reporting regime.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last"><div class="glossary-term">Interim Financial Reporting (ASBJ Statement No. 37)</div><div class="glossary-def">The current successor framework governing Japan's semi-annual statutory financial reporting obligation.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表) <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書) <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部 <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書) <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</div></div>

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
